      "id": "138-initial-components",
      "operation": "precise-object-edit",
      "prompt": "Use case: precise-object-edit, production animation source components, not a finished sticker. Create ONE transparent PNG with FOUR equal square quadrants in a 2x2 grid, no text, no labels, no dividers. Use Images 1 and 2 to preserve the exact same cream-and-turquoise mouse-like character, rounded ears, large blue eyes, navy cape and amber-gold round clasp, with a playful white ghost costume. Image 3 is identity reference for the correct TWO small upper central front teeth: no side teeth, no lower teeth. Keep the existing polished soft 3D sticker look. Every quadrant is a separate clean animation layer with generous transparent margins and no overlap across quadrant borders. TOP LEFT: the full-body character from Image1, ears/head/face/belly/feet/cape/clasp and white hood side drapes preserved; remove BOTH arms and paws entirely, reconstruct the small regions of cloak and hood behind them naturally. Face fully visible, warm mischievous smile showing exactly two upper front teeth. This is an underlying armless body animation plate; no detached stumps, arms are hidden under the cape. TOP RIGHT: ONLY one isolated left arm from shoulder to large open paw, cream fur with turquoise paw tips and blue paw pads facing viewer, matching Image1's waving arm; short rounded forearm aimed down-right toward its shoulder, no body/head/other objects. BOTTOM LEFT: ONLY one isolated right arm from shoulder to gently curved gripping paw, same fur/shading, palm inward, short rounded forearm aimed down-left, no body/head. BOTTOM RIGHT: ONLY an opaque white draping front veil panel, matching the white fabric covering the face in Image2. Soft triangular hanging shape with curved top and curved lower hem, about 1.15 times taller than wide, visible cloth folds, a SINGLE painted ghost face (two dark oval eyes and one small dark oval mouth) on its front. No actual eyes, no character, no hands, no clasp, no legs, no ears behind or through this cloth. The cloth must be fully opaque inside its silhouette; background transparent. Do not add extra characters or props. Keep every isolated layer complete inside its own quadrant and on an actual transparent background. The components will later be composited and rigged; anatomically consistent source layers are essential.",
